Avx_runner was designed to detect NVMesh kernel module AVX registers corruption.
The test loads AVX2 / AVX512 registers with non zero random values
and verifies that values in these registers did not change over time

The test will not run if AVX512 instruction set is not supported

The test executable receives the following optional command line parameters:
-t <sec> number of seconds to run the test. If the -t parameter was omitted, 
the test will run 10 sec. The test will not run more then 100 hr. 
The test will immediately terminate on corruption discovery.
-v dump mathematics to screen
-y AVX2 test
-z AVX512 test
